@startuml Sequence_ReportSummary
title SQL Report Summary Aggregate — No Hydration (v0.9.3)

actor Merchant
participant "ReportPage" as UI
participant "GetReportSummary" as UC
participant "SaleRepository" as Repo
participant "SaleQueryLocalDatasource" as DS
database "SQLite\n(sales + sale_payments)" as DB

Merchant -> UI: Select date range + "Summary"
UI -> UC: call(from: startDate, to: endDate)
UC -> Repo: getReportSummary(from: startDate, to: endDate)
Repo -> DS: queryReportSummary(from: startDate, to: endDate)

group Single SQL Aggregation Pass
    DS -> DB: SELECT\n  COUNT(*),\n  SUM(net_amount_satang),\n  SUM(voided_total_satang),\n  SUM(vat_amount_satang),\n  SUM(discount_amount_satang),\n  SUM(service_charge_satang),\n  SUM(promotion_discount_satang),\n  SUM(CASE WHEN status='VOIDED' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)\nFROM sales\nWHERE deleted_at IS NULL\n  AND created_at BETWEEN from AND to
    DB --> DS: aggregated totals (INTEGER satang)

    DS -> DB: SELECT payment_method,\n  SUM(amount_satang), COUNT(*)\nFROM sale_payments\nWHERE sale_id IN (chunked 500-row batches)\nGROUP BY payment_method
    DB --> DS: payment breakdown + counts

    DS -> DB: SELECT order_type, SUM(net_amount_satang)\nFROM sales ... GROUP BY order_type
    DB --> DS: order type breakdown

    DS -> DB: SELECT order_channel, SUM(net_amount_satang)\nFROM sales ... GROUP BY order_channel
    DB --> DS: order channel breakdown

    DS -> DB: SELECT void_reason, COUNT(*)\nFROM sales WHERE status='VOIDED' ... GROUP BY void_reason
    DB --> DS: void reason breakdown
end

DS -> DS: Build ReportSummary\n(satang → Money via Money.fromSatang)\nREAL baht fallback for pre-v32 rows
DS --> Repo: ReportSummary
Repo --> UC: ReportSummary
UC --> UI: ReportSummary
UI --> Merchant: Render summary card\n(net revenue, voids, VAT, discounts,\npayment breakdown, order type/channel)

note over DS, DB
  **No List<Sale> hydration** — all metrics
  computed in SQL. Item-derived metrics
  (top products, profit/margin) still
  require the existing hydration path.
  Payment method lookup is chunked to 500
  rows to stay under SQLite's 999-variable
  limit.
end note

@enduml
